there is breaking news overnight about  syria where u.s special operations  forces carried out a counter-terrorism  rate moments ago president biden said  the troops took the leader of isis off  the battlefield rescue workers in syria  say at least 13 people died david martin  has more from the pentagon crumbling  concrete and rubble is evidence of the  deadly u.s special operations raid  carried out overnight in syria  it happened in the town of atma not far  from the turkish border  an area of northwest syria known as a  hotbed for terrorist organizations  reports from residents on the ground say  the raid lasted two hours and involved  helicopters explosives and machine gun  fire  in a statement the pentagon said the  mission was successful which should mean  the target was killed or captured there  were no u.s casualties but a defense  official said one helicopter broke down  and had to be destroyed and left behind  according to residents and activists u.s  troops used loudspeakers urging women  and children to leave the area  there was at least one explosion  it was the largest u.s raid in syria  since the 2019 operation that killed  islamic state leader abu bakr  al-baghdadi who blew himself up rather  than be captured the pentagon has not  yet identified the target of this raid  although it comes just days after the  islamic state stage a major attack on a  prison camp which holds some 3 000 of  its members  for cbs morning's david martin
 

